        "id": 1042638
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-06-12T23:30:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If the worker can\u0027t start, there must be an error, so this check is redundant, we can just use `getError`. This will also eliminate the need for exposing `hasError`.",
